    "SMART SYSTEM"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Boiler",
  "applies_to": "Lochinvar Power-fin PB/PF 'X' models 502-1302 and 1501-2001 with the SMART SYSTEM control and Modbus/BACnet communication board, per PBX-PFX-MODB Rev D.",
  "summary": "Older-generation Lochinvar Power-fin boilers and water heaters with the SMART SYSTEM control talk Modbus RTU through an RS-485 communication board. The BAS writes a configuration word, an enable word, a rate or setpoint command and optional remote temperatures; it reads switch and flame states, outlet/inlet/flue temperatures, firing rate, cascade power, status/blocking/lockout codes and cascade members' lockout codes.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": null,
    "data_bits": null,
    "stop_bits": null,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "Addresses are printed Modicon-style (00001, 10001, 30001, 40001). Subtract the table base and 1 for the wire address; the manual's exception-code text confirms PDU addresses start at 0."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "ModBus and BACnet Communication Instructions - Power-fin Models 502-1302; 1501-2001",
    "doc_number": "PBX-PFX-MODB 100161633_2000016132 Rev D",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://assets.lochinvar.com/damroot/Original/10014/PBX-PFX-MODB_100161633_2000016132_REV%20D_BACNET(56304).pdf",
    "pages": "pp. 3-6 (Modbus configuration, exception codes), 7-8 (memory map, configuration bits), 18-21 (unit operation, conversions), 22-23 (codes)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Temperatures: the conversion section says the Power-fin passes temperatures in degrees C and the value must be divided by 10 (examples: 26.7 C sent as 267; outlet 683 = 68.3 C). Scale 0.1 is applied to the temperature registers with 0.1 resolution in the map.",
    "Left out: System/Cascade Setpoint (30004), Outlet Setpoint (30008) and Tank Setpoint (40004). The map gives them a 0.5 C resolution while the conversion text says temperatures are C x 10, so their scaling is not settled.",
    "Signed types: inlet, flue and BAS-supplied temperatures have negative minimums in the map and are listed as INT16; the manual itself only says 16-bit word.",
    "Input registers 30001-30003 and 30026 are packed copies of the discrete inputs; the bit order is not stated, so they are UINT16. Use the discrete inputs instead.",
    "Lockout code 234 and 236 are both printed as 'Air Pressure Switch stuck open'; both are kept as printed.",
    "This is the older PBX/PFX (SMART SYSTEM) board. Newer Power-fin boards have a separate manual and are not covered here."
  ],
